    "kind": "sea",
    "name": "Lower Sea (Persian Gulf) c. 1750 BC",
    "note": "Approximate head of the Gulf c. 1750 BC. The mid-Holocene maximum transgression (c. 6000-5000 BP) reached roughly the Nasiriyah-Amara line near Ur/Eridu (Sanlaville; Aqrawi; Heyvaert & Baeteman); delta progradation then pushed the coast south-east, reaching roughly its modern position by the 1st millennium BC (Sauvage atlas). Here the c. 1750 BC shoreline is placed ~60-80 km NW of today's, around the Basra-Zubair-Khorramshahr area, with brackish lagoons/marsh between it and Ur-Eridu. Lees & Falcon (1952) argued for little change; the true line is uncertain by tens of km. The polygon extends beyond the map bbox into the Gulf."
   },
